{"name":"Lost River","hex":"#08457e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Lost River","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A locality in the Upper Lachlan council area, south eastern New South Wales, Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Lost_River"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lost River, New South Wales","blocks":[{"text":"Lost River is a locality, in the Upper Lachlan Shire, within the Southern Tablelands of New South Wales, Australia. It lies on either side of the main road between Crookwell and Boorawa, which are the nearest towns to it."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lost_River%2C_New_South_Wales"},{"title":"Harrington, Quebec","blocks":[{"text":"Harrington is a township municipality in the Laurentides region of Quebec, Canada, part of the Argenteuil Regional County Municipality. It is located in the Laurentian Mountains, about 40 kilometres (25 mi) north-west of Lachute."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Harrington_Twp_QC.JPG/330px-Harrington_Twp_QC.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harrington%2C_Quebec"},{"title":"Lost River (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Lost River is a 2014 American fantasy thriller film written, co-produced, and directed by Ryan Gosling, in his feature directorial debut. The film stars Christina Hendricks, Saoirse Ronan, Iain De Caestecker, Matt Smith, Ben Mendelsohn, Barbara Steele, and Eva Mendes."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/22/Lost_River_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lost_River_(film)"},{"title":"River","blocks":[{"text":"A river is a natural stream of fresh water that flows on land or inside caves towards another body of water at a lower elevation, such as an ocean, lake, or another river. A river may run dry before reaching the end of its course if it runs out of water, or only flow during certain seasons. Rivers are regulated by the water cycle, the processes by which water moves around the Earth. Water first enters rivers through precipitation, whether from rainfall, the runoff of water down a slope, the melting of glaciers or snow, or seepage from aquifers beneath the surface of the Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg/330px-Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/QC_Harrington1_tango7174.jpg/500px-QC_Harrington1_tango7174.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/QC_Harrington1_tango7174.jpg/1280px-QC_Harrington1_tango7174.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/QC_Harrington1_tango7174.jpg/500px-QC_Harrington1_tango7174.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Buddhist Monastery of Tam Bao Son in the Township of Harrington.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AQC_Harrington1_tango7174.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/NorthAmerica-WaterDivides.png/500px-NorthAmerica-WaterDivides.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/NorthAmerica-WaterDivides.png/500px-NorthAmerica-WaterDivides.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The major drainage basins in North America","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANorthAmerica-WaterDivide